<title>UK: UK Treasury confirms Brown to meet George on May 7.</title>
<headline>UK Treasury confirms Brown to meet George on May 7.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Treasury confirmed on Friday that new Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown will meet Bank of England governor Eddie George on May 7 for a scheduled monetary meeting.</p>
<p>Markets are focused on the regular monetary meeting, believing it could result in a small rise in interest rates.</p>
<p>Britain's newly-elected Labour Prime Minister Tony Blair earlier confirmed Brown as chancellor in his new cabinet.</p>
</text>
